  "kind": "fixture",
  "readme": [
    "SYNTHETIC CATALOGUE \u2014 a test fixture, NOT sourcing truth.",
    "",
    "Every part below is invented to exercise the selection engine: there is one that qualifies,",
    "and one for each way a part can fail (the OTHER family's clock, 5 V part, unplaceable",
    "package, no published phase noise, too noisy, single-sourced). The MPNs are deliberately",
    "prefixed FIXTURE- so they can never be mistaken for parts anyone researched or can order.",
    "",
    "FIXTURE-OSC-24M576-WRONGFAMILY is the interesting one. 24.576 MHz is a perfectly good",
    "CS43131 MCLK \u2014 the DAC accepts it for every rate the product supports \u2014 and it is the",
    "cheapest, deepest-stocked, most-sourced oscillator here. It still has to be rejected for the",
    "44.1 kHz family, because the SAI cannot divide it to an exact 64 x 44100 bit clock",
    "(24.576e6 / 2.8224e6 = 8.707...). That is a constraint belonging to the MCU's serial port,",
    "not to the DAC, which is exactly the distinction an earlier version of this spec got wrong.",
    "",
    "The real catalogue replaces this file wholesale once distributor credentials exist: the",
    "fetcher pulls every part in a category from TME / Mouser / Digi-Key, and the engine filters",
    "it with exactly the same constraints exercised here. Nothing about the engine changes when",
    "the data becomes real \u2014 which is the point of testing it against a fixture first.",
    "",
    "Attribute names match what parametric search returns (frequency_hz, supply_mv_max, package,",
    "phase_noise_dbc_1khz, channels, break_before_make, max_freq_hz), because the constraints in",
    "dap-hw-spec are written against that vocabulary rather than an invented one.",
    "",
    "The battery and bluetooth categories exist because several constraints on those parts are",
    "LICENSING constraints wearing electrical clothing, and they are the ones a price-first",
    "filter gets wrong. FIXTURE-CELL-1200-SOLDERTAB is the cheapest cell with the deepest stock",
    "and the largest capacity, and it has to lose: solder tabs mean no spare battery and no",
    "Art. 11 user-replaceability. FIXTURE-CELL-1100-BARE is cheaper still and would transfer",
    "UN 38.3 and IEC 62133-2 certification from the cell vendor to us. FIXTURE-BT-BARE-SOC is",
    "half the price of the qualified module and costs a full Bluetooth qualification programme.",
    "",
    "REWRITTEN 2026-11-24 to the vocabulary real distributors actually publish, after the first",
    "live TME fetch showed the old fixture had invented its own. Supply voltage is a RANGE",
    "(supply_mv_min/max) because that is how it is published, and the constraint is containment",
    "of the 3.3 V rail rather than a ceiling. Mux parts are described by switch_configuration",
    "(SPDT) and channels counted as SWITCHES, which is TME's convention.",
    "",
    "Note what is NO LONGER here: a part failing on break_before_make or max_freq_hz. Those are",
    "datasheet facts that no distributor publishes, so the catalogue filter cannot test them and a",
    "fixture part 'failing' on them tested nothing but the fixture's own invention.",
    "",
    "Oscillators rewritten 2026-11-24 after surveying all 121 parts TME returns for 22.5792 and",
    "24.576 MHz. Two findings shaped it. First, the vendor category MIXES passive parts (crystal,",
    "ceramic, resonator) with active ones (oscillator, XO) under 'Type of quartz', so the",
    "discriminator is a real catalogue-checkable constraint and the fixture carries both kinds.",
    "Second, NO part in that survey publishes phase noise or jitter in any form \u2014 so phase noise",
    "is a datasheet obligation, not a filter, and a fixture part 'failing' on it tested nothing.",
    "",
    "moq added 2026-11-24. FIXTURE-OSC-22M5792-B is now reel-only (1000), modelled on the real",
    "Abracon ASV-22.5792MHZ-LR-T: 17000 in stock, 0.70 EUR each, and a 1000-piece minimum that",
    "makes it a 700 EUR line item for a part a prototype needs one of.",
    "",
    "Batteries rewritten 2026-11-24 to TME's rechargeable-battery vocabulary, after sweeping all",
    "70 Li-Po cells it carries. The discriminators are what the vendor actually publishes:",
    "'Rechargeable batteries features' naming 'PCB protection' (the integrated-PCM condition the",
    "certification argument rests on), 'Leads' naming the JST connector (what makes a spare",
    "swappable), and 'Rated voltage' of 3.7 V which IS the 1S statement \u2014 a cells-in-series count",
    "is published nowhere.",
    "",
    "Note what is NO LONGER here: a cell failing on dimensions or on UN 38.3 / IEC 62133-2 docs.",
    "TME publishes neither, so those are datasheet obligations and a fixture part 'failing' on",
    "them tested nothing but the fixture's own invention.",
    "",
    "Bluetooth rewritten 2026-11-24 after sweeping 100 real pre-certified modules from Digi-Key \u2014",
    "the first candidates this requirement ever had. The failure modes are now the ones a",
    "CATALOGUE can judge: package ('Module' versus a bare QFN), supply-range containment of the",
    "3.3 V rail, and mounting.",
    "",
    "Gone: parts failing on bt_sig_qualified, requires_vendor_nda or codec_sbc. A QDID and an NDA",
    "status are certificates, not parametric fields \u2014 no distributor publishes them, so those are",
    "datasheet obligations and a fixture part 'failing' on them tested only the fixture."
  ],
